In this part of Lam Rim, Pabongka Rinpoche said,

00:11:45.760 --> 00:11:52.160
“The place where you should spread the Dharma is here, in your heart.”

00:11:52.240 --> 00:11:57.560
Don't think that spreading the Dharma means translating videos

00:11:57.560 --> 00:12:02.120
into multiple languages ​​or anything like that.  This is a very important spread of the Dharma.

00:12:02.920 --> 00:12:06.680
But, he says, "If you spread Dharma within your heart,

00:12:07.280 --> 00:12:11.280
then of course it will spread outside of you because the world comes from your heart."

00:12:11.280 --> 00:12:13.000
From the heart chakra, actually.

00:12:13.760 --> 00:12:18.200
Next image #7

00:12:20.720 --> 00:12:24.720
Try to remember what this image was about.  I'll leave you for a second.

00:12:29.960 --> 00:12:33.000
This is a favorite topic of mine:

00:12:33.680 --> 00:12:43.400
having a personal relationship with another person, like these two people have.

00:12:45.080 --> 00:12:49.200
In my opinion and in tantra, it is one of the happiest things that can happen to you.

00:12:49.200 --> 00:12:53.200
It's one of the greatest things that can happen to you.

00:12:54.120 --> 00:12:59.000
Anyone can tell you the reason why the whole world is looking for a partner.

00:12:59.840 --> 00:13:01.480
The reason is that it makes people happy.

00:13:01.480 --> 00:13:04.720
It is one of the greatest joys when things go well.

00:13:05.840 --> 00:13:09.000
It's one of the greatest joys you can have, but

00:13:09.840 --> 00:13:14.120
we both know that when it doesn't go well,

00:13:15.000 --> 00:13:17.560
it's one of the greatest misfortunes in life.

00:13:18.320 --> 00:13:21.200
Why is this relevant to this course here?

00:13:25.200 --> 00:13:30.520
If your morality is good,

00:13:30.720 --> 00:13:32.800
it is the happiest thing in your life.

00:13:33.400 --> 00:13:38.440
And if you violate your morality, the same thing will make you unhappy.

00:13:38.680 --> 00:13:41.760
It's like having a man or woman you like who is your partner,

00:13:42.720 --> 00:13:46.120
and the same person who makes you completely happy

00:13:46.160 --> 00:13:49.200
can also make you completely unhappy.

00:13:49.720 --> 00:13:53.840
So in this case, the vinaya, your personal practice of being good to others,

00:13:54.320 --> 00:13:57.680
your good behavior, is compared to a partner

00:13:57.680 --> 00:14:01.120
who can be the best thing in your life

00:14:01.760 --> 00:14:04.760
or the worst thing in your life - the same person.

00:14:05.440 --> 00:14:11.520
Next IDIM #8

00:14:12.920 --> 00:14:15.200
That was a complicated one.  Can you remember?  I'm going to

00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:19.000
take a sip of my green drink.

00:14:20.160 --> 00:14:22.160
Thank you, Vimala.

00:14:30.920 --> 00:14:35.040
This actually represents breaking your commitments.

00:14:35.440 --> 00:14:41.040
Pulling out a weed represents breaking your commitments.

00:14:41.080 --> 00:14:46.680
Why is destroying this plant a breach of commitment?

00:14:46.920 --> 00:14:53.040
If you're a gardener, you know you should pull a weed out of the ground

00:14:53.920 --> 00:14:56.160
before the seeds ripen.

00:14:56.880 --> 00:15:00.920
If you wait until the seeds are ready to fall,

00:15:01.360 --> 00:15:03.280
and then pull the plant out of the ground,

00:15:03.560 --> 00:15:06.040
you will scatter about a thousand seeds.

00:15:07.000 --> 00:15:12.680
Next month or next year you'll get thousands of weeds growing.

00:15:12.680 --> 00:15:14.920
So, you will need to attack these weeds early.

00:15:15.960 --> 00:15:20.560
This refers to a very radical statement

00:15:20.800 --> 00:15:22.800
that the Buddha made:

00:15:23.400 --> 00:15:29.240
@DGE SLONG DAG SROG DANG BRAL ZHING SHI BA NI BLA'I

00:15:29.680 --> 00:15:31.680
It says that it is better to die

00:15:31.760 --> 00:15:33.960
than to break your vows.  Why?

00:15:35.000 --> 00:15:37.000
When you break your vows

00:15:37.080 --> 00:15:40.360
you set in motion seeds

00:15:40.520 --> 00:15:44.160
that will continue to fall for many lifetimes.

00:15:44.720 --> 00:15:51.080
If you die, you destroy a single mind-body entity.

00:15:51.960 --> 00:15:55.440
If you die, you destroy only one very useful temple,

00:15:55.440 --> 00:15:58.800
a physical temple and a mind.  You lost one life.

00:16:00.040 --> 00:16:02.040
But if you break your vows,

00:16:02.720 --> 00:16:05.920
you lose more mind-body ensembles.  You are

00:16:05.920 --> 00:16:08.920
destroying your body and mind for many lifetimes.

00:16:09.680 --> 00:16:12.920
And you have set in motion seeds

00:16:12.920 --> 00:16:15.720
that will destroy many lives.

00:16:15.800 --> 00:16:21.880
Buddha said, "It is better to die than to break your vows," and he

00:16:22.080 --> 00:16:28.920
wasn't being metaphorical.  He was speaking literally

00:16:28.920 --> 00:16:32.720
when he said that.  Better to die than to break your commitments.

00:16:34.800 --> 00:16:36.800
There is a joke in Lam Rim.

00:16:38.240 --> 00:16:45.760
We make a vow to never give up bodhichitta even at the cost of our lives.

00:16:48.040 --> 00:16:53.960
There is a famous statement, our whole lives we wait

00:16:54.040 --> 00:16:56.040
to be thrown in jail

00:16:56.240 --> 00:16:58.240
by certain bad people.

00:16:58.600 --> 00:17:03.960
They come with a knife and say, "Give up your bodhisattva vows or die today."

00:17:04.520 --> 00:17:06.120
We will tell [them]:

00:17:06.120 --> 00:17:07.960
"I choose to die."  And they kill us

00:17:07.960 --> 00:17:10.600
.

00:17:11.080 --> 00:17:14.720
I think we've all been waiting for this since we took that oath.

00:17:15.560 --> 00:17:19.720
We're waiting for these guys with knives to show up and threaten us.

00:17:19.720 --> 00:17:24.320
But actually we're the guys with the knives.  We threaten our bodhisattva vows every day.  We

00:17:26.000 --> 00:17:33.200
must make this decision every day when we decide whether or not to keep our vows carefully.

00:17:36.280 --> 00:17:39.200
It's hard to find the guys who will throw you in jail and say,

00:17:39.440 --> 00:17:42.920
"I'll kill you if you don't give up your bodhisattva vows."  The

00:17:46.040 --> 00:17:48.040
next picture.

00:17:49.480 --> 00:17:56.040
See if you remember.  I'll give you a minute to try to remember.

00:18:05.200 --> 00:18:07.200
This was a reference....

00:18:07.400 --> 00:18:10.440
we have the Mixed Nuts translation team

00:18:11.200 --> 00:18:14.040
and we were translating an old vinaya text.

00:18:15.200 --> 00:18:17.920
The vows of monks, the vows of nuns.

00:18:18.520 --> 00:18:26.560
They were talking about the vow, the custom that you shouldn't...

00:18:26.800 --> 00:18:31.160
...When you become a monk or nun you're given robes, they

00:18:31.200 --> 00:18:33.200
give you a little Buddhist statue,

00:18:34.320 --> 00:18:36.320
and they give you a strainer.

00:18:37.280 --> 00:18:40.720
In ancient India you had to carry this strainer with you.

00:18:41.480 --> 00:18:44.800
When drinking water from a stream you

00:18:45.400 --> 00:18:50.920
should strain the water first to make sure you don't kill any small insects.

00:18:51.840 --> 00:18:57.000
I mentioned a famous custom in the vinaya,

00:18:57.680 --> 00:19:00.680
if two monks go down to the water,

00:19:00.960 --> 00:19:03.840
down to the stream to get water,

00:19:04.160 --> 00:19:08.800
then they should choose the most benevolent monk to check the water.

00:19:10.720 --> 00:19:16.440
Don't choose the one who doesn't care about insects.  Find a guy who loves bugs

00:19:17.200 --> 00:19:20.720
and have him check the water because he'll be more careful.

00:19:21.400 --> 00:19:23.400
What's the idea?

00:19:24.160 --> 00:19:27.920
We talked about a type of ecological vow,

00:19:28.440 --> 00:19:33.040
where monks and nuns are not supposed to even pull the leaves of

00:19:33.080 --> 00:19:39.040
a plant, because they are shelter for small creatures.

00:19:39.440 --> 00:19:44.400
This means - to respect even very small vows,

00:19:44.400 --> 00:19:50.600
take them very seriously, because the results multiply exponentially.

00:19:50.600 --> 00:19:55.080
Then, it's important to keep your morality at a very subtle level,

00:19:56.440 --> 00:19:59.840
at a very fine level, and don't analyze them.

00:20:02.040 --> 00:20:04.040
If I were to write the bodhisattva vows, I

00:20:04.040 --> 00:20:06.040
would write an additional bodhisattva vow about

00:20:06.440 --> 00:20:08.600
not analyzing your bodhisattva vows.  There

00:20:09.200 --> 00:20:11.200
's nothing more irritating than

00:20:11.840 --> 00:20:15.880
a person informing you that they're honoring their vows and that's why they

00:20:15.880 --> 00:20:19.080
have to be insensitive today.

00:20:21.080 --> 00:20:24.600
Keep your vows in a pleasant way.  Keep them being happy.  Don't exaggerate.

00:20:25.200 --> 00:20:31.080
Don't bother other people with your vows because vows are not meant to bother other people.

00:20:32.040 --> 00:20:36.720
Keep vows small, keep them quiet.  Keep them to yourself, don't advertise them.

00:20:37.760 --> 00:20:43.560
There is a saying in Islam... Let the left hand not know what the right hand is doing.

00:20:44.440 --> 00:20:48.120
That means not advertising your vows.  Keep them quiet.

00:20:48.920 --> 00:20:51.200
Keep them at a very fine level.  The

00:20:52.040 --> 00:20:54.040
next picture.

00:21:00.680 --> 00:21:06.120
Here is the idea that being kind to others

00:21:06.520 --> 00:21:10.240
is like planting a tree.

00:21:10.600 --> 00:21:13.400
Today I went to the Peach Tree Cafe

00:21:13.520 --> 00:21:16.080
to check something out.

00:21:17.400 --> 00:21:20.440
Stanley, Allison, and I planted a peach tree there

00:21:22.160 --> 00:21:25.080
when we first started the morning show, "The Peach Tree."

00:21:25.840 --> 00:21:29.760
And I want to tell you that three peaches came out this week.

00:21:30.520 --> 00:21:32.800
And now we have peaches.

00:21:35.080 --> 00:21:40.160
That means taking care of basic practices.

00:21:40.160 --> 00:21:44.560
Take care of your roots and plant beautiful karma

00:21:45.200 --> 00:21:47.920
by keeping your vows and being kind to others.

00:21:47.920 --> 00:21:49.960
And this will turn into a tree.

00:21:50.440 --> 00:21:52.440
And that peach tree that I planted

00:21:53.200 --> 00:21:55.080
about five months ago is

00:21:55.080 --> 00:21:58.040
already bearing a lot of fruit.

00:21:58.600 --> 00:22:05.040
If you hadn't taken care of it when it was small [the tree], you would have nothing [now].

00:22:05.040 --> 00:22:08.200
If you take care of the foundation of your Buddhist practice,

00:22:08.800 --> 00:22:10.800
which is being kind to other people,

00:22:11.400 --> 00:22:14.120
then the fruits will be thousands and thousands and thousands.

00:22:14.200 --> 00:22:16.160
[The result] will come, it will grow

00:22:16.160 --> 00:22:18.160
...it will turn into a tree

00:22:18.600 --> 00:22:23.480
that will bear peaches every year and you will have fruit for many years.

00:22:24.160 --> 00:22:25.560
Preserve... protect...

00:22:25.760 --> 00:22:29.560
This child carefully protects the shoot.

00:22:29.960 --> 00:22:31.960
Protect your morality.  [Keep your morals]

00:22:32.520 --> 00:22:34.520
Next picture.

00:22:36.240 --> 00:22:41.320
If I remember correctly, there were four conditions

00:22:42.240 --> 00:22:45.080
that could cause you to break your commitments.

00:22:45.080 --> 00:22:47.080
If you've taken your bodhisattva vows

00:22:47.840 --> 00:22:50.440
or you've taken your pratimoksha vinaya vows,

00:22:51.000 --> 00:22:53.840
or even if you've taken your tantric Diamond Way vows

00:22:54.800 --> 00:23:00.200
... I think there were four... ...that Pabongka Rinpoche reviewed... maybe more....

00:23:01.000 --> 00:23:02.920
However, there are certain conditions

00:23:03.000 --> 00:23:05.080
that can "help" you break your vows.

00:23:05.160 --> 00:23:09.240
If you want to break your vows, there are a few ways to do it.  The

00:23:09.240 --> 00:23:10.320
first way

00:23:11.080 --> 00:23:16.440
is to not know the vows

00:23:17.120 --> 00:23:21.000
and that's a good way to break them.  If you want to break them,

00:23:21.000 --> 00:23:22.720
then don't study them and

00:23:23.160 --> 00:23:27.080
one of the things that bothers me... I have a lot of things that annoy me about the Dharma,

00:23:28.160 --> 00:23:33.800
is teachers who give initiations, huge initiations,

00:23:33.800 --> 00:23:38.600
and they don't explain to the people they're initiating

00:23:39.080 --> 00:23:41.520
that they've just taken vows.

00:23:41.560 --> 00:23:44.840
There are hundreds of vows you take when you receive an initiation,

00:23:45.760 --> 00:23:48.320
and you will [certainly] break them if you don't know them.

00:23:48.320 --> 00:23:51.120
It is the teacher's responsibility to

00:23:52.120 --> 00:23:55.400
prepare you regarding the vows before giving you an initiation.

00:23:56.320 --> 00:24:01.080
If they don't offer to train me, [I] wouldn't accept an initiation from them.

00:24:02.120 --> 00:24:07.080
The best way to break your vows, the first way, is to not know them.

00:24:07.560 --> 00:24:09.400
Read the recipe before you start cooking.

00:24:10.240 --> 00:24:12.720
That's what Veronica tells me every time I cook.  The

00:24:14.160 --> 00:24:16.160
next picture.

00:24:17.000 --> 00:24:23.360
There's a lady who says, "Hey, it's no big deal."

00:24:23.560 --> 00:24:33.600
That vow about cutting down green plants without saying a prayer,

00:24:34.320 --> 00:24:40.400
seriously, that's a bit of an exaggeration.  It's a bit too much, it's not that important.

00:24:40.400 --> 00:24:43.000
There are just a few insects

00:24:43.000 --> 00:24:47.560
that might use that leaf from time to time as a roof.  It's no

00:24:47.560 --> 00:24:50.040
big deal.

00:24:50.480 --> 00:24:53.800
The second great way to break your vows

00:24:54.040 --> 00:24:55.400
is to have this attitude.

00:24:55.400 --> 00:24:59.200
"Oh, this oath is not that important, I keep the big ones."

00:25:00.200 --> 00:25:02.120
Next.

00:25:06.240 --> 00:25:12.400
If we have a klesha, meaning if we have some kind of negativity

00:25:12.800 --> 00:25:16.920
running through our mind, that's a very good way to break your vows.

00:25:17.080 --> 00:25:20.600
Being irritated by someone else or

00:25:21.080 --> 00:25:26.280
being obsessed with purchasing something or money or

00:25:26.600 --> 00:25:29.480
being addicted to watching Netflix at night.

00:25:30.040 --> 00:25:36.000
...By the way, it's not wrong to watch Netflix [movies], I'm talking about

00:25:38.960 --> 00:25:43.200
hurting someone else because you want to get home and watch Netflix.  That's a problem.

00:25:44.800 --> 00:25:46.920
This is called gang warfare.

00:25:46.920 --> 00:25:48.320
What is the story about?

00:25:52.120 --> 00:25:56.040
Always go after the biggest guy on the opposing side.

00:25:57.000 --> 00:25:59.000
Find out who the leader of the other side is,

00:25:59.560 --> 00:26:04.080
and don't talk, don't negotiate, don't yell at each other,

00:26:04.080 --> 00:26:07.000
just go up to him and hit him in the head.

00:26:07.480 --> 00:26:10.800
And then all the others [his colleagues] will give up.

00:26:11.080 --> 00:26:15.080
Identify your biggest bad habit,

00:26:15.080 --> 00:26:19.000
and go for it first.  That's how you take your vows.

00:26:19.760 --> 00:26:21.760
Next.

00:26:25.240 --> 00:26:30.640
...By the way, at my age, I wo

00:26:30.640 --> 00:26:33.760
n't tell you how old I am,

00:26:33.760 --> 00:26:37.080
but this whole young love thing

00:26:37.080 --> 00:26:40.160
is so ridiculous from the perspective of my age.

00:26:42.320 --> 00:26:44.800
I can say it from experience, because I had it.

00:26:46.320 --> 00:26:48.240
This...

00:26:48.240 --> 00:26:50.800
"Oh, she's the most beautiful woman in the world."

00:26:51.400 --> 00:26:53.400
"He's the most handsome guy in the world."

00:26:54.440 --> 00:26:59.560
First of all, my older brother

00:26:59.560 --> 00:27:02.920
said the funniest thing.  He said, "Do you like that girl?"  I said, "Yes."  He

00:27:03.480 --> 00:27:05.480
said, "Do you want to spend your life with her?"  I said, "Yes."

00:27:06.160 --> 00:27:08.160
He said, "First look at her mother."

00:27:09.000 --> 00:27:16.120
"Look at what her mother looks like." I said [her] mother looks terrible.  She's overweight, looks tired, and looks terrible.

00:27:16.920 --> 00:27:21.800
And he said to me, "Well, what do you think he looked like when he was young?"

00:27:22.040 --> 00:27:24.240
Think about this.

00:27:25.480 --> 00:27:29.560
If you are attached to a person's appearance,

00:27:30.240 --> 00:27:35.280
or to something physical, or to something that is not very important about a person,

00:27:35.480 --> 00:27:41.120
that appearance will change and you will see them get sick, you

00:27:41.120 --> 00:27:44.000
will see them get old, you will see them have diarrhea and vomit.

00:27:44.240 --> 00:27:48.040
If you're not lucky, at some point you'll see his entrails or on the operating table.  Do

00:27:49.080 --> 00:27:52.120
n't fool yourself into thinking

00:27:53.080 --> 00:27:55.080
that it's worth hurting other people

00:27:55.760 --> 00:28:00.680
to get the most beautiful woman or man you can have.  It's not worth it.  It won't

00:28:01.960 --> 00:28:08.600
last.  It's great to have a relationship, but have it for the right reason.

00:28:09.200 --> 00:28:11.200
Next.

00:28:13.000 --> 00:28:15.080
If you have an anger problem

00:28:16.160 --> 00:28:18.160
or get angry easily,

00:28:18.320 --> 00:28:21.080
then imagine giving that person

00:28:21.760 --> 00:28:25.480
something they would like to have.  This is called @maitre

00:28:26.120 --> 00:28:27.480
@jampa

00:28:27.480 --> 00:28:28.120
Love.

00:28:28.120 --> 00:28:33.400
Imagine, try to remember how nice it is to give someone

00:28:34.040 --> 00:28:36.160
something they like, something they want.

00:28:36.200 --> 00:28:38.240
Try to have this attitude.

00:28:38.720 --> 00:28:42.040
If you don't feel friendly towards another person,

00:28:43.000 --> 00:28:45.880
then imagine what it would be like to meditate on

00:28:47.000 --> 00:28:50.440
what it would be like to give them something they really like.

00:28:51.000 --> 00:28:53.000
Next.

00:28:54.040 --> 00:29:00.040
I'll give you a moment for this... I bet you don't remember what this is...

00:29:01.480 --> 00:29:03.400
Tim cheats by looking ahead.

00:29:08.040 --> 00:29:10.040
What was that?  It's

00:29:11.080 --> 00:29:13.960
about pride.

00:29:14.720 --> 00:29:17.840
Pride is also an obstacle to keeping vows.

00:29:18.720 --> 00:29:22.120
And... one of the most common kinds of pride

00:29:23.000 --> 00:29:28.040
in a monastic setting, where this book was generally taught,

00:29:30.320 --> 00:29:35.280
is how much you know about the scriptures and how much data you have gathered

00:29:36.040 --> 00:29:37.120
throughout your life.  I

00:29:37.400 --> 00:29:41.280
really like that.  These Dharma teachings are very little known

00:29:41.280 --> 00:29:43.080
and the more you collect them, the

00:29:43.480 --> 00:29:47.080
more special you feel.

00:29:48.040 --> 00:29:52.960
Pabongka Rinpoche said, "All the Dharma you have ever learned in your life, all the things you have memorized,

00:29:52.960 --> 00:29:54.720
all the things you have debated,

00:29:54.720 --> 00:29:56.800
all the Geshe degrees you could ever have,

00:29:58.480 --> 00:30:04.160
compared to what is left to study... you know nothing."

00:30:04.480 --> 00:30:07.560
You are like a worm at the bottom of the ocean,

00:30:08.240 --> 00:30:10.120
which sometimes comes to the surface and looks at the stars.

00:30:13.000 --> 00:30:15.680
Many of these stars have planets around them.

00:30:16.520 --> 00:30:20.440
There are people on those planets.  There are things to know about these people.

00:30:21.400 --> 00:30:24.480
Here are the things we know,

00:30:24.720 --> 00:30:26.720
that we are so proud to know,

00:30:27.680 --> 00:30:33.880
they are a tiny tiny [very] tiny fraction of what you could know.

00:30:35.160 --> 00:30:37.200
So, don't be proud!

00:30:37.200 --> 00:30:39.200
Next.

00:30:43.000 --> 00:30:47.240
One of the great motivations for breaking your vows

00:30:47.680 --> 00:30:54.240
or commitments, morality, that will stop you from reaching nirvana, that will stop you from reaching

00:30:55.080 --> 00:30:57.680
the second level of Larm Rim -- personal nirvana --

00:30:58.720 --> 00:31:03.000
is to understand emptiness, to study emptiness.

00:31:04.320 --> 00:31:06.320
If you realize that the bad things

00:31:06.920 --> 00:31:08.920
someone else does to you

00:31:09.480 --> 00:31:13.240
come directly from what you did last week,

00:31:13.960 --> 00:31:18.240
then you won't make big mistakes.  The more you study emptiness,

00:31:19.000 --> 00:31:22.440
the more you study cause and effect, interdependence,

00:31:23.000 --> 00:31:25.280
which means that that person comes from my seeds,

00:31:26.360 --> 00:31:33.760
then the easier it will be for you to keep your vows.  It will be much easier for you.  So study, study, study!  I

00:31:35.560 --> 00:31:41.320
had a very old Mongolian professor who had tuberculosis and

00:31:46.800 --> 00:31:48.720
he would say,

00:31:48.720 --> 00:31:56.240
"That's good. You're so proud, you have such a huge amount of pride from Princeton and

00:31:57.080 --> 00:31:58.720
then the fact that you're a geshe,

00:31:58.720 --> 00:32:00.800
it's a big help, a big help... You're

00:32:00.880 --> 00:32:03.960
going to push yourself so hard

00:32:04.440 --> 00:32:06.440
just to look smart.

00:32:06.520 --> 00:32:11.600
That's luck, but later try to give it up.

00:32:11.960 --> 00:32:15.080
Study how to be a good person. It's very funny.

00:32:16.080 --> 00:32:19.000
On his deathbed, he gave me the text that Adam is translating. I

00:32:19.760 --> 00:32:21.760
remember that. The

00:32:24.040 --> 00:32:25.960
next one

00:32:25.960 --> 00:32:30.320
Technically is that the fourth cause? No.

00:32:30.440 --> 00:32:35.480
One of the causes of breaking vows or commitments

00:32:37.560 --> 00:32:39.680
is that in the modern world it's very hard

00:32:40.120 --> 00:32:45.960
to think about vows when you're so busy. When things are moving so fast.

00:32:46.520 --> 00:32:48.920
There's a thousand things to look at on the internet

00:32:49.680 --> 00:32:53.000
and life is moving so fast.

00:32:53.440 --> 00:32:58.640
It's hard to keep your self-awareness. Am I

00:32:58.640 --> 00:33:03.080
breaking my vows, doing things that hurt others?

00:33:03.840 --> 00:33:08.680
I have to  slow down, go back to your vows.

00:33:09.080 --> 00:33:14.720
And maintain a sense of awareness

00:33:15.000 --> 00:33:19.880
that you have commitments not to hurt others.

00:33:20.080 --> 00:33:24.160
The busier you are, the more mindful you need to be.

00:33:25.680 --> 00:33:31.000
It's even easier to get annoyed with your partner when you're really busy.

00:33:31.000 --> 00:33:33.200
He's trying to tell you something and

00:33:33.960 --> 00:33:36.320
you have 10 things going on at work and...

00:33:37.840 --> 00:33:42.120
"I don't have time to listen right now.  "My

00:33:42.800 --> 00:33:45.960
boss gave me 10 things to do."

00:33:46.440 --> 00:33:48.440
Those are the times when you need to slow down

00:33:49.200 --> 00:33:51.200
and come back to your vows.

00:33:51.280 --> 00:33:55.000
Don't forget your commitment to be nice to other people, even when you're

00:33:55.680 --> 00:33:57.680
really stressed, really busy.

00:33:59.960 --> 00:34:04.440
It's better to break a few business commitments than to

00:34:05.760 --> 00:34:10.040
get angry and stressed and not be nice to people.

00:34:11.200 --> 00:34:14.040
It's better to not pay a bill or miss a business meeting or

00:34:15.000 --> 00:34:17.560
not give your best at work

00:34:18.720 --> 00:34:21.960
if it means keeping your mind clear.

00:34:25.080 --> 00:34:27.080
Next picture.

00:34:27.480 --> 00:34:30.840
This is a lady buying something she doesn't need at the store.

00:34:33.200 --> 00:34:35.200
See if you remember this story.

00:34:36.800 --> 00:34:42.160
She said, "Oh, this box is so beautiful." She went to the store. She bought it...

00:34:42.600 --> 00:34:44.600
...What's that home improvement store, the

00:34:45.080 --> 00:34:48.480
place where you buy things for the home? Crate and Barrel.

00:34:49.000 --> 00:34:54.040
She went to Crate and Barrel in America. She said, "Oh, my husband is going to love this box."  She

00:34:54.520 --> 00:34:57.480
has no idea what she's going to use it for,

00:34:58.040 --> 00:35:00.040
but she's going to buy it.

00:35:04.320 --> 00:35:09.400
And when she gets home, her husband will say, "You're crazy, this is a worthless box."

00:35:09.400 --> 00:35:15.480
"We have enough junk in the house."  "Take her back."  "Get your money back."

00:35:16.920 --> 00:35:20.720
Should she go to the gas station and try to return it?

00:35:24.120 --> 00:35:29.760
No, that's not where she got the box. It's obvious, but we have to say it.

00:35:31.480 --> 00:35:33.480
If you buy a stupid box

00:35:34.040 --> 00:35:37.080
because you like it and you think your husband will like it, which he won't...

00:35:39.000 --> 00:35:41.080
and he convinces you to take the box back,

00:35:42.040 --> 00:35:46.160
don't take it back somewhere else. Take it back to where you bought it.

00:35:46.720 --> 00:35:48.720
What does that mean? You should

00:35:55.480 --> 00:35:58.080
pay me.

00:35:59.680 --> 00:36:01.680
When you have to confess

00:36:01.680 --> 00:36:03.480
because you broke a vow,

00:36:03.480 --> 00:36:06.120
try to go to the person who made you the vow.

00:36:07.080 --> 00:36:12.120
Confess to the person who made you the vow.

00:36:12.200 --> 00:36:15.960
Is it okay to confess alone at home?

00:36:17.680 --> 00:36:21.960
No, for vows that you took from other people, generally.

00:36:24.040 --> 00:36:26.040
If you didn't take a vow

00:36:26.040 --> 00:36:28.600
from someone else, then maybe it's okay to confess at home,

00:36:29.280 --> 00:36:34.080
confess in front of a Buddha statue or something. In extreme cases, it's okay.

00:36:34.440 --> 00:36:36.120
But,  In general,

00:36:36.520 --> 00:36:39.080
if you can go back to the person who made your vows

00:36:40.160 --> 00:36:45.200
and confess openly, do it shamelessly. We act shamelessly all day long.

00:36:45.840 --> 00:36:49.080
So be shameless when it comes to your vows, and say to yourself, "What the hell!"

00:36:49.960 --> 00:36:52.720
Go straight to your teacher and say, "I broke this stupid vow."

00:36:53.200 --> 00:36:56.720
And your teacher will say, "Wow, you're a really bad person."  You're like... "

00:36:57.400 --> 00:37:02.040
Get over it and then you'll feel so clean, you'll feel so good.

00:37:03.520 --> 00:37:07.320
You can be shy about a lot of things in your life, but don't be shy about your vows.

00:37:07.320 --> 00:37:11.000
If you break a vow, go tell someone

00:37:11.000 --> 00:37:14.240
and [that's] how you get rid of the... Get rid of the problem.

00:37:14.520 --> 00:37:20.000
If you hide it from yourself and if you work harder to hide it than to confess it

00:37:20.040 --> 00:37:23.200
or to keep your vow, then it's just stupid

00:37:23.480 --> 00:37:26.600
and you're not going to feel good. You're not going to feel clean.

00:37:27.480 --> 00:37:31.760
Be open with your teachers. I have this problem. I have this bad habit.

00:37:33.560 --> 00:37:37.720
The karma is broken, the seed is broken.

00:37:38.320 --> 00:37:44.920
Your teacher will say, "I've heard that before, you told me before." But be persistent and keep telling them.

00:37:48.320 --> 00:37:50.320
Next picture:

00:37:51.840 --> 00:37:54.320
It's about... Wait! Remember?

00:38:01.160 --> 00:38:04.200
Again, it's about honoring the

00:38:04.800 --> 00:38:07.480
little details of the vows.

00:38:08.400 --> 00:38:13.680
It's actually  a vow for monks, they should brush their teeth,

00:38:13.680 --> 00:38:16.320
with a stick called @SO SHING.

00:38:16.320 --> 00:38:18.440
It was a stick that you have to use to clean your teeth. You

00:38:18.600 --> 00:38:21.280
cut it out of a tree and you use it.

00:38:22.160 --> 00:38:24.160
It's a toothbrush.

00:38:24.320 --> 00:38:29.360
It's said that these monks should have their own toothbrushes and brush their teeth. It

00:38:31.840 --> 00:38:34.040
might seem like a small thing.

00:38:34.920 --> 00:38:38.920
"Wait, I'm trying to keep my tantric vow to go to Amitabha's paradise

00:38:39.560 --> 00:38:43.080
and protect all living beings."  and Buddha says, "Yes, but in the meantime,

00:38:43.080 --> 00:38:46.240
you could brush your teeth every day."

